%I A398824 #16 Aug 12 2026 01:36:38
%S A398824 4,8,9,12,16,18,20,24,25,27,28,32,36,40,44,45,48,49,50,52,54,56,60,63,
%T A398824 64,68,75,76,80,81,84,88,90,92,96,98,99,100,104,112,116,117,120,121,
%U A398824 124,125,126,128,132,135,136,140,144,147,148,150,152,153,156,160,162,164
%N A398824 Numbers whose powerful part (A057521) is a perfect power that is larger than 1.
%C A398824 First differs from its subsequence A375142 at n = 53: a(53) = 144 is not a term in A375142.
%C A398824 Nonsquarefree numbers k such that A057521(k) is a term in A001597.
%C A398824 Each term in this sequence has a unique representation as the product of two coprime numbers: a squarefree number and perfect power that is larger than 1.
%C A398824 The asymptotic density of numbers whose powerful part is an m-th power (m >= 2), is d(m) = zeta(m) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 - 1/p^(m+1) + 1/p^(m+2)).
%C A398824 The asymptotic density of the subsequence of this sequence that includes only terms whose powerful part is an m-th power that is larger than 1 (m >= 2), is d(m) - 1/zeta(2).
%C A398824 The asymptotic density of this sequence is -Sum_{m>=2} mu(m) * (d(m) - 1/zeta(2)) = 0.3695478374078823155157..., where mu is the Möbius function (A008683).
%H A398824 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398824/b398824.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398824 <a href="/index/Eu#epf">Index entries for sequences computed from exponents in factorization of n</a>.
%e A398824 12 = 2^3 * 3 is a term since its powerful part, 4 = 2^2, is a perfect power that is larger than 1.
%t A398824 q[k_] := Module[{e = Select[FactorInteger[k][[;;, 2]], # > 1 &]}, Length[e] > 0 && GCD @@ e > 1]; Select[Range[165], q]
%o A398824 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(e = select(x -> x > 1, factor(k)[,2])); #e > 0 && gcd(e) > 1;}
%Y A398824 Subsequences: A375142, A398820, A398822.
%Y A398824 Cf. A001597, A008683, A013661, A013929, A057521, A059956.
%Y A398824 Numbers whose powerful part is: A005117 (1), A048107 (1 or square of a prime), A048109 (cube of a prime), A060687 (square of a prime), A067259 (square of a squarefree number), A274034 (terms in A322449), A335275 (square), A336591 (cube of a squarefree number), A337050 (cubefull number), A375142 (power of a squarefree number that is larger than 1), A398818 (cube), A398820 (square larger than 1), A398822 (cube larger than 1), this sequence (perfect power larger than 1).
